looking for ways to break down data  silos and enable analytics over data  regardless of where it's stored give me  one minute and i'll show you how with  google cloud big lake  big lake is a storage engine that  extends bigquery storage capabilities  such as fine-grained security  performance caching and sharing to open  formats on multi-cloud object stores  enabling organizations to unify data  warehouses and lakes  maintain a single copy of your data  wherever you choose and make it  uniformly accessible across google cloud  and open source engines including  bigquery vertex ai spark presto trino  and hive using big lake connectors  big lake capabilities extend to data no  matter how it's stored including popular  open data formats such as parquet avro  orc csv and json  queries on big lake tables provide  industry-leading performance powered by  the same technology that underlies  bigquery  apply table row and column level  security policies on object store tables  without having to provide file level  access to end users  big lake integrates with dataplex  allowing you to provide unified  governance and management at scale  you can interact with big lake through  its integrations with other google cloud  products for example you can create  discover and query big lake tables from  the bigquery console  you can do the same thing through a  dataproc notebook  so if you're looking to unify  distributed data and enable analytics  governance and management at scale  take a minute to look at big lake  to learn more check out cloud.google.com  [Music]  you
 

